+SRE Oncall Playbook (short)
+===========================
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Provide a concise guide for oncall engineers to respond to incidents for Aegis platform services.
+
+Oncall triage flow
+1. Alert received (PagerDuty/Grafana)
+2. Identify impacted service (model-server, hil-scheduler, rt-wcet, etc.)
+3. Access dashboards (Grafana links) and logs (ELK/Cloud logs)
+4. Run quick health checks:
+   - kubectl get pods -n aegis-ml
+   - ops/tests/integration/ci_gate_check.py (local)
+5. If hardware-related (HIL/RT/NPUs), check ops/tests/staging/lab_manager.py registry for node status and contact hardware-owner.
+6. Escalate to release/safety owner if evidence/signed artifacts are implicated.
+
+Incident resolution
+- Restore service (restart pods, scale down/up).
+- If deterministic failures observed (HIL), preserve artifacts (do not delete) and tag evidence with legal_hold if needed.
+- Run mitigation runner (ops/mitigation/mitigation_runner.py) for recovery steps (if configured).
+
+Post-incident
+- Create incident ticket with timeline, root cause, artifacts and corrective actions.
+- Add to postmortem board and follow backlog items in ops/runbooks/prioritized_backlog.yml.
+
